<title>UK: ABBEY NAT UPS MORTGAGE RATES 25 BASIS PTS.</title>
<headline>ABBEY NAT UPS MORTGAGE RATES 25 BASIS PTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank Abbey National Plc said on Friday it is increasing its standard variable mortgage rates by 25 basis points.</p>
<p>The increase will take effect from August 11 for new customers and from</p>
<p>September 1 for existing mortgage customers.</p>
<p>Abbey National said in a statement from September 1, its standard</p>
<p>variable mortgage for existing borrowers will be --</p>
<p>			    NEW RATE	    OLD RATE</p>
<p> Up to 59,999 stg   8.45 percent	8.20 percent</p>
<p> 60,000 stg	   8.40 percent	8.15 percent</p>
<p> 100,000 stg	  8.35 percent	8.10 percent</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of England's decision on Thursday to raise UK interest rates to 7.00 percent from 6.75 percent.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
